---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// Apple requires a support URL on every App Store listing, and KAMO had none — the other
// six apps point at per-app Notion pages that live outside this repo. This is a plain,
// versioned support page so the listing has somewhere real to send people.
//
// A static route rather than part of [app]/: the other apps already have their own support
// destinations, and inventing pages for them here would silently compete with those.
---

<Base
  title="KAMO Support | Bliss Coach"
  description="Help with KAMO — the camouflage camera toy. Contact, common questions, and how to manage your subscription."
  bodyClass="article-page"
>
  <article>
    <header class="article-header">
      <h1>KAMO Support</h1>
      <p class="meta">Camouflage camera toy — iOS</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Something broken, confusing, or missing? Email
        <a href="mailto:anthony@blisscoach.app">anthony@blisscoach.app</a> and you'll get a
        reply from a person. Telling us your iPhone model and iOS version makes it much
        faster to reproduce.
      </p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>

      <h3>The camera is black, or KAMO never asks for permission</h3>
      <p>
        KAMO needs camera access to work at all. Open iOS Settings &rsaquo; KAMO and turn
        <strong>Camera</strong> on. If you denied it the first time, that switch is the only
        way back — the app cannot ask twice.
      </p>

      <h3>Saving to my camera roll does nothing</h3>
      <p>
        Check iOS Settings &rsaquo; KAMO &rsaquo; Photos and allow adding photos. KAMO only
        ever writes the image you just made; it never reads your library.
      </p>

      <h3>The torch button does nothing</h3>
      <p>
        The light needs a device with a rear flash, and it only lights while the camera view
        is open. On models without one, the button doesn't appear.
      </p>

      <h3>I paid and KAMO+ isn't unlocked</h3>
      <p>
        Tap <strong>Restore</strong> on the paywall — purchases follow your Apple ID, so this
        also covers a new phone or a reinstall. Make sure you're signed in with the same
        Apple ID you bought with. If it still doesn't unlock, email us with the date of
        purchase.
      </p>

      <h3>Managing or cancelling a subscription</h3>
      <p>
        Subscriptions are billed by Apple, not by us, so they're managed in iOS Settings
        &rsaquo; your name &rsaquo; Subscriptions. Cancel at least 24 hours before the period
        ends to avoid renewal. Refunds are handled by Apple at
        <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/" rel="nofollow">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.
        The Lifetime unlock is a one-time purchase and never renews.
      </p>

      <h3>What happens to my photos</h3>
      <p>
        They stay on your phone. KAMO paints the camera frame on-device and never uploads it
        — the full detail is in the <a href="/kamo/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Legal</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/kamo/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> &middot;
        <a href="/kamo/terms/">Terms of Use</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
